   "Because the blue whale is a mammal, as you are. It breathes air, and it feeds its young on milk. A newborn blue whale calf drinks hundreds of litres of its mother's milk a day, and puts on weight at a rate that would alarm any health visitor. The biggest mammal on Earth does not live on land at all. Which rather puts the rest of us in our place. Blue whales can live for eighty or ninety years, and much of what they say to each other is pitched too low for human ears.",
   "And it once did live on land, in a manner of speaking. Whales are descended from four-legged land mammals that waded into the shallows some fifty million years ago. Their closest living relatives are hippopotamuses. Some whales still carry a few small hip bones, deep inside the body, left over from legs they stopped using a very long time ago.",
